{
  "comment": "ISS-1405: shared with the Mac writer. Each case lists the files of one ledger directory and the record a write or delete targets (`target`, the canonical id; `ref`, the id or display id a user passes). `hint`: refused with misnamedRecordMessage(target, dir, files[0]). `collision`: refused with misnamedCollisionMessage(target, dir, files). `allowed`: the write goes ahead. `duplicate`: the load also carries ISS-1404's duplicate_id, so a strict lock refuses first with that message. The unknown case (a directory or record that cannot be read) refuses too; it is built by the test, not listed here.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "legacy ticket under another name",
      "dir": "tickets",
      "files": [
        {
          "name": "T-001 old.json",
          "id": "T-001"
        }
      ],
      "target": "T-001",
      "ref": "T-001",
      "expected": {
        "verdict": "hint",
        "files": [
          ".story/tickets/T-001 old.json"
        ]
      },
      "duplicate": false
    },
    {
      "name": "legacy issue under another name",
      "dir": "issues",
      "files": [
